{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_7wijene2d7jxltybkzwqv7edlejqem2clmkwzfu4euc2vpdrgbga","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification is complete. All four phases pass, and I found and fixed one real bug.\n\n## Completion gate\n\n- **`SYMBOLS.md`** — `nm -D` diff is **empty**: the C `.so` exports 10 symbols (`c2V`, `c2Maxv`, `c2Minv`, `c2Clampv`, `c2Sub`, `c2Dot`, `c2CircletoCircle`, `c2CircletoAABB`, `c2AABBtoAABB`, `collided`) and the Rust `.so` exports exactly those 10. No module was missing, nothing stubbed. `cargo check` was clean from the start.\n- **Phase B** — all **33/33** `CONFIGS.md` rows pass, 4000 fixed-seed random inputs per row, compared on **bit patterns** (so NaN payloads and signed zeros count).\n- **Phase C** — all **12/12** `ERRORS.md` rows pass, plus a sentinel test proving `collided`'s `0` came from the `default:` arm rather than a plain miss.\n- **All profiles/features** — `Cargo.toml` declares no `[features]`, so `feature_matrix.sh` derives the matrix from the manifest and runs `default` × `--no-default-features` × dev/release: 51 tests each, all passing.\n\n## The bug (Phase C, row 7)\n\n`collided` dereferences its `const void *` unconditionally. The translation used `read_unaligned`, so with a null pointer:\n\n| | Rust (before) | C (ground truth) |\n|---|---|---|\n| debug / UB-checked `.so` | **SIGABRT** — non-unwinding panic, *\"unsafe precondition(s) violated\"* | SIGSEGV |\n| release `.so` | SIGSEGV | SIGSEGV |\n\nEvery ordinary spelling has this problem — `ptr::read`, `read_unaligned`, `read_volatile`, `copy_nonoverlapping` (hence also `repr(packed)` field reads) carry `assert_unsafe_precondition!`, and even plain `*(p as *const T)` picks up rustc's *\"null pointer dereference occurred\"* check. Fixed by loading each `float` with a single `mov` via `core::arch::asm!`, which is what gcc emits anyway; this also removes the alignment assumption, matching C's unchecked misaligned reads.\n\n## Two things worth flagging\n\n1. **`cargo test` does not rebuild a cdylib-only library** — no test target links it. My first Phase B/C runs silently tested a *stale* `.so`, which is how a false pass happens. `tests/common/mod.rs::assert_not_stale` now compares mtimes and fails loudly, and `run_all.sh` always builds first.\n2. **The C's own NaN output is build-flag dependent** in `c2Dot`. The Rust matches the `-O0` ordering that `c_src/CMakeLists.txt` actually produces (`mulss` dst=`a.x`/`b.y`, `addss` dst=y-product). I verified against a `gcc -O2` build: 32/33 rows still pass, and the only difference needs **two or more distinct NaN payloads** in one call. Documented in `CONFIGS.md`; the Rust is pinned to the specified build.\n\nI also added `tests/harness_sanity.rs` (proves via `/proc/self/maps` that each function pointer lives in its own `.so`, so the tests genuinely cross the FFI boundary into two different libraries) and `mutation_check.sh`, which breaks the Rust 12 different ways and confirms each is caught — notably `checked_null_read` is caught *only* in the debug profile, which is why both profiles are always run."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":643,"cache_read_input_tokens":171565,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":643,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b9caa612-3da8-4ef4-be37-a3e27f28d555","uuid":"a4a34dba-0832-4f72-95c4-924360dd5821","timestamp":"2026-08-26T20:11:02.265Z"}
